Mutation-hardening drill. Save /workspace/leap.py:

def is_leap(year):
    if year % 400 == 0:
        return True
    if year % 100 == 0:
        return False
    return year % 4 == 0

and /workspace/tests/test_leap.py containing only:

from leap import is_leap

def test_common():
    assert is_leap(2024)
    assert not is_leap(2023)

The following mutants must all be killed by the suite: M1: 400 -> 100. M2: 100 -> 400. M3: first return True -> return False. M4: second return False -> return True. M5: % 4 == 0 -> % 4 != 0. Add the minimal set of test cases that kills all five (think 2000, 1900, plus what you already have), then prove it: a python script mutate_check.py that programmatically writes each mutant (string replacement on the source, applied one at a time), runs pytest with the mutant on sys.path front, and reports killed/survived per mutant. All five KILLED, original green, and print a one-line summary table.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])
